{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790516001,"nonce":"EqJc6BOPH44rI5vlOy0R2pKIuSE=","message":"Wire generated (34aed77, 60687b8). caribou_bindgen::idl parses the whole IDL with weedle2; weedle2 lacks namespace constants, so a constants-only namespace is read as an interface. caribou_bindgen::wire::wire(idl) -\u003e Wire { rust, js } writes both halves, and the module doc there gives the encoding. For webgpu.idl, every operation, attribute and setlike whose values the wire can encode is included; operations with browser-only types (HTMLVideoElement, callbacks, events) are left out, and optional members of such types are dropped from dictionaries. tests/wire_node.rs compiles the generated Rust with rustc, encodes a session (requestAdapter, requestDevice, queue, createBuffer, writeBuffer with bytes in shared memory), and runs the generated ES module under Node against a recording GPU. The calls, arguments, replies and handles all come out right. Still to do here: cb_gpu's build writing gpu_wire.rs and the agent module (with ec051e6 and 451cc06), and moving the older generate() off the hand tokenizer onto the model.","files":null}]}